# What `fastapi deploy` uploads to FastAPI Cloud, on top of .gitignore (which
# already drops .env, .venv, caches, logs and build outputs; `!pattern` would
# un-ignore). The API needs only interview_agent/, alembic/ with alembic.ini,
# main.py, pyproject.toml and uv.lock; the rest below is the web app, the
# worker's container, Terraform, tests, scripts and docs. Two files stay on
# purpose: .python-version, so the platform builds with the same interpreter
# as the local venv and the Docker image, and README.md, because pyproject's
# `readme` points at it and the build on the platform reads it.
web/
infra/
tests/
scripts/
.github/
Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
.env
.env.*
secrets*.env
logs/
*.log
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.DS_Store
.gitattributes
README*
*.md
!README.md
